### Backend Changes

#### [MODIFY] [vault.ts](file:///c:/Users/misal/OneDrive/Documents/next-framer/trpc/routers/vault.ts)

Minimal server-side changes (the server is intentionally dumb about encryption):

- `createItem`: Accept new optional fields `encryptedPassword`, `encryptedContent`, `encryptedPlainText`, `encryptionIv`. When present, store these instead of plaintext. Store a flag `isEncrypted: true` on the item.
- `updateItem`: Same — accept encrypted variants.
- `formatItem`: Pass through encrypted fields to the client. The client decrypts.
- `getPublicItems`: Continue stripping passwords. For encrypted private items, they'll never appear here anyway.

Add a new procedure:
- `getEncryptionSalt` / `setEncryptionSalt`: Store/retrieve the user's PBKDF2 salt (this is safe — salt is not secret, it's just unique per user)

